  "title": "Quiche alsacienne",
  "subtitle": "Alsatian bacon and cream tart in a crisp shortcrust shell",
  "excerpt": "Quiche alsacienne is the original Alsatian version of the cream tart before the term quiche lorraine became the catch-all name. It differs from its Lorraine counterpart by including caramelised onions alongside the bacon, which gives the filling a sweeter, more rounded flavour. The custard is rich double cream and eggs; there is no cheese in the authentic version. Blind-bake the pastry shell fully before filling so the base stays crisp.",
  "type": "RECIPE",
