  "season": null,
  "sourceType": "CLASSIC",
  "sourceNotes": "Quiche alsacienne is a savoury cream tart from the Alsace region of France (historically under alternating French and German rule). The earliest printed quiche recipes are documented in 19th-century Alsatian cookery books under the name Küche (from the German word for cake). The classic Alsatian preparation is distinguished from quiche lorraine by the inclusion of onions (Zwiebelkuchen in the German tradition) and the use of crème fraîche. The recipe is documented in Elizabeth David's French Provincial Cooking (1960) and Richard Olney's Simple French Food (1974).",
