      "term": "Blind baking",
      "definition": "Baking a pastry case empty before adding the filling. The case is lined with baking paper and filled with baking beans or rice to prevent it from puffing up. Blind baking ensures the base cooks through and stays crisp under a wet filling such as a custard tart."
