  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Quiche alsacienne is a three-stage recipe: make and chill the pastry, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "techniqueLink",
                "attrs": {
                  "techniqueSlug": "blind-baking",
                  "label": "blind-bake"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blind-bake"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " it fully, then add the filling. Skipping or shortening the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blind-baking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "blind bake"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is the most common cause of a soggy quiche base. The onions need at least 20 minutes over a gentle heat to soften and sweeten; rushing them gives a bitter result."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
