              "groupLabel": "Filling"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make and chill the pastry"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rub {{unsalted-butter}} (100 g) into {{plain-flour}} and {{sea-salt-fine}} until the mixture resembles coarse breadcrumbs. Add {{water}} one tablespoon at a time, pressing the dough together until it just coheres. Do not overwork. Wrap and refrigerate for 30 minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Line and blind-bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 190°C (conventional). Roll the pastry on a lightly floured surface and line a 24 cm loose-bottomed tart tin. Trim any overhang. Prick the base, line with baking paper, fill with baking beans, and blind-bake for 20 minutes. Remove the beans and paper, then bake for a further 10 minutes until the base is pale golden and dry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cook the bacon and onions"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fry {{streaky-bacon}} in a large frying pan over a medium heat until the fat renders and the lardons begin to turn golden, about 5 minutes. Remove with a slotted spoon. Add 20 g {{unsalted-butter}} to the pan and add {{onion}}. Cook over a very low heat, stirring occasionally, for 20 to 25 minutes until very soft, sweet, and pale golden but not browned. Spread the onions and bacon over the blind-baked tart base."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the custard and bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Reduce the oven to 175°C (conventional). Whisk {{double-cream}}, {{eggs}}, {{egg-yolks}}, {{nutmeg}}, and {{sea-salt-fine}} together until smooth. Pour over the onions and bacon in the tart shell. Bake for 30 to 35 minutes until the custard is just set with a slight wobble in the very centre. Leave to rest for 15 minutes before unmoulding. Serve warm or at room temperature."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
